  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Coordination for Disaster Response in Nigeria (ECoDIN) Program - COOPI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Enhancing Coordination for Disaster Response in Nigeria (ECoDIN) Program seeks to strengthen relevant government institutions and systems to better plan and respond to human-induced or natural disasters in selected locations in Northcentral, Nigeria.&#xa0;


The main objective of the program is to enhance government capacity and systems to better manage shocks and improve coordination of disaster response.&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0;


The outcome of the project will be improved/strengthened government systems to detect, manage, and respond to shocks in the selected states. It will be a continuous learning action that helps to transform humanitarian actions into development interventions while institutions responsible for disaster management and humanitarian responses will have their capacity enhanced for state-wide coverage and response as required.</narrative>
  </description>
